A||N||12||Roy||Got Smoked By A 2000 Celica GTS||||4||
Z||000000||Roy||01-20-2000||06:54 AM||||I was coming home from work today about midnight. I was waiting at the onramp light to the highway, when a blue 2000 celica gts pulled up next to me. He started to rev his engine, so I rev'd my 88 gt's. As soon as that light turned green I floored it through first. I beat him off the line, but that didn't mean much by the time I was about to shift out of second he was right next to me. After second gear he blew me away. *mutter*, Well I guess I'm proud I beat him off the line. But other than that, that was the worst I've ever been smoked. But I guess I gotta look at it in performance terms, that car can rev too 7k, has a 6 spd tranny. Its got 180hp:P, hmm wouldn't mind getting my hands on that engine:P<P>Roy <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||ChadMan||01-20-2000||08:37 AM||||He may be faster, but from every angle but the front, the new Celica is butt-ugly.  And that "new edge" styling will be old hat in five years.  A Fiero GT was beautiful in 1988, it's beautiful now, and it will be beautiful 20 years from now.<P>Plus, if you really, really need to be faster, you can spend 1/3 the purchase price of a new Celica on a Northstar conversion!||||reg||1
Z||000002||loafer87gt||01-20-2000||09:11 AM||||Actually, that little beast has 7800 RPM redline. Must sound like your riding a chainsaw! Would be kinda cool though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||01-20-2000||02:28 PM||||There are a LOT of newer cars (and some trucks) that will blow away a stock Fiero in a drag race.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>There are not near as many that will keep up on a twisty road.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Straight line racing never was the Fiero's strong point. It's only gotten worse as more cars get high tech, high HP engines.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WGraffiKs||01-20-2000||04:10 PM||||Thanks, Chad!  You took the "butt-ugly" words right out of my mouth!  But what do you mean, from every angle but the front?  They look like a sawed-off butt THERE, too!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Remember, everyone, we have engines with early-to-mid-80's technology. None of that multiple valve, twin O/H cam stuff here.  I know most of you guys are young, and prefer the drag-race mentality, but curves is what the Fiero is all about.  That's why it was made with so many of them!  I love the look of the forlorn silly-Ka gee-tea owner as he/she stares at my "Pontiac" emblem (tail) disappearing around the next bend!!! If you gotta drag, put a little $ into the engine, you will be much happier than a $broke silly-Ka owner, AND look better to boot!<p>[This message has been edited by WGraffiKs (edited 01-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||01-20-2000||08:26 PM||||Im going on the assumption that your 88 GT is still running the same engine it came with. I would imagine that it has some miles on it and would not be considered a "fresh" engine. After 12 years you are still able to put it through a drag race? <P>Let see how the Sell-It-Ca is doing in 2012....<P>Oh and don't worry, if that Celica is in Southern California feeling like he can beat any Fiero, there are a few Fieros in our club that would love to just suck the doors off that Toyota. We just LOVE doing that....||||reg||14
Z||000006||doughboySE||01-20-2000||09:32 PM||||hey guys am i the only 32 year old fiero owner that would rather cruz and show off the style of my baby then race down the street to try and prove what an awsome car we have? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> i have to admit i have challenged my fare share but ill tell you after spending 6-8 hours every sunday detailing and waxing my pride and joy i seem to turn more heads as my car slowly drives by and changes from gold to light violet to white <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>and you can read there lips<BR>MAN NICE CAR WHAT KIND OF CAR IS THAT <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>the young kids love the ride <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||01-21-2000||12:53 AM||||Its good to have a cruiser, some of us just believe in the saying, "Pretty is as Pretty does." <P>Not all the time to be sure. But I sure have a hard time resisting some punk Honda trying to call me out...<P>I wouldn't call it racing...racing is being competitive...||||reg||6
